From 340439b390b991a59f20fecb7e61f995a13e73a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon West <electrikjesus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:48:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Taskbar: Keep system bar apps clear of the buttons and
 the tray

In desktop mode the taskbar start-aligns its icons after space meant
for end-side nav buttons, so on the tablet system bar they covered
back/home/recents and the extra buttons. Lay them out between the
start buttons and the tray instead, at the start, center (default) or
end per persist.retro.ui_bar_apps_gravity, and add no extra buttons
unless persist.retro.ui_bar_buttons lists them.

Change-Id: Ia674ae4ebcd4185be10e13b59753b00eba6cc084
---
 quickstep/res/values/retro_system_bar.xml     |  2 +
 .../taskbar/NavbarButtonsViewController.java  |  1 +
 .../launcher3/taskbar/RetroSystemBar.kt       | 72 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarView.java        |  4 ++
 4 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

